WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.895 --> 00:00:16.757
squeezed Nina's hand and smiled.

2
00:00:17.757 --> 00:00:20.018
She loved to go to the woods during summer camp.

3
00:00:21.739 --> 00:00:23.440
Today the campers had a mission.

4
00:00:24.461 --> 00:00:26.282
They were looking for wildflowers!

5
00:00:26.302 --> 00:00:28.883
"How do we know what to pick?"

6
00:00:29.304 --> 00:00:30.004
Izzie asked.

7
00:00:31.892 --> 00:00:35.373
"We don't want to pick flowers growing on a vine or bush.

8
00:00:36.473 --> 00:00:40.214
So look for flowers growing on the ground from one stem.

9
00:00:41.435 --> 00:00:44.596
Big flowers with thick petals will be best," Mr.

10
00:00:44.636 --> 00:00:45.276
Dunn said.

11
00:00:45.296 --> 00:00:47.997
"Is this one good?"

12
00:00:48.237 --> 00:00:49.037
Bobby asked.

13
00:00:50.277 --> 00:00:53.358
Bobby pointed to a white flower the size of a fingernail.

14
00:00:56.839 --> 00:00:59.732
"No, silly," said Izzie.

15
00:00:59.752 --> 00:01:02.033
"You need something bigger and darker, right, Mr.

16
00:01:02.073 --> 00:01:04.293
Dunn?" The teacher nodded.

17
00:01:08.314 --> 00:01:09.215
look at this!"

18
00:01:10.315 --> 00:01:12.656
Izzie squatted next to two purple flowers.

19
00:01:18.117 --> 00:01:19.298
they're so pretty!

20
00:01:19.318 --> 00:01:22.738
I love the color," Nina gushed.

21
00:01:22.758 --> 00:01:24.979
"Can we pick these, Mr.

22
00:01:24.999 --> 00:01:26.460
Dunn?" Izzie asked.

23
00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:27.960
"You may.

24
00:01:28.884 --> 00:01:31.045
Those look perfect," said Mr.

25
00:01:31.085 --> 00:01:33.807
Dunn. The girls each picked one.

26
00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:37.469
"Here are some!"

27
00:01:37.849 --> 00:01:38.650
Jason called.

28
00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:42.712
He pointed to the same kind of flowers Izzie had found.

29
00:01:43.732 --> 00:01:45.093
But his were bright yellow.

30
00:01:46.074 --> 00:01:47.534
And there were only three of them.

31
00:01:48.555 --> 00:01:51.096
Izzie rushed over, pushing Jason aside.

32
00:01:51.116 --> 00:01:53.178
"Let me get one!"

33
00:01:53.538 --> 00:01:57.360
"Izzie." She felt a firm hand on her arm.

34
00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:02.527
"This is not a competition, and we do not push," Mr.

35
00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:03.168
Dunn said.

36
00:02:03.188 --> 00:02:10.673
"Sorry." Izzie watched grumpily as Jason, Ethan, and Bobby picked their flowers.

37
00:02:10.693 --> 00:02:15.076
"Jackpot!" Ethan cried.

38
00:02:17.918 --> 00:02:19.979
He pointed to a small circle of color.

39
00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:26.244
It was made up of flowers—dark purple, light purple, and yellow flowers!

40
00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.141
"You only need two flowers," Mr.

41
00:02:30.181 --> 00:02:30.801
Dunn said.

42
00:02:30.821 --> 00:02:33.322
"Don't pick more than that.

43
00:02:34.442 --> 00:02:38.063
Flowers are living plants, and their home is here in nature."

44
00:02:39.003 --> 00:02:40.204
But Izzie ignored him.

45
00:02:44.285 --> 00:02:46.165
Quickly she picked six flowers.

46
00:02:50.746 --> 00:02:54.007
Back in the gym, everyone placed their flowers on the table.

47
00:02:55.288 --> 00:02:56.168
Izzie had seven.

48
00:02:57.032 --> 00:02:58.373
Everyone else had two.

49
00:02:58.393 --> 00:03:03.455
"We're going to make hammered flower artwork," said Mr.

50
00:03:03.495 --> 00:03:06.276
Dunn. "I'll explain as we work.

51
00:03:09.037 --> 00:03:12.538
I gave everyone two pieces of watercolor paper.

52
00:03:13.639 --> 00:03:17.300
So you can only use two flowers," said Mr.

53
00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:21.502
Dunn. He looked at Izzie sharply, and then continued.

54
00:03:21.522 --> 00:03:25.143
"Place one flower on the watercolor paper.

55
00:03:26.204 --> 00:03:28.498
Then place a paper towel on top.

56
00:03:29.999 --> 00:03:36.144
Using your hammer, gently pound your flower.

57
00:03:36.164 --> 00:03:39.687
Then lift up the paper towel to see what's left," Mr.

58
00:03:39.748 --> 00:03:40.728
Dunn continued.

59
00:03:40.768 --> 00:03:45.833
Izzie chose her favorite flower and began pounding.

60
00:03:50.957 --> 00:03:53.780
When she pulled back her paper towel, she gasped.

61
00:03:56.492 --> 00:03:59.054
"It looks like a stamp," Izzie exclaimed.

62
00:03:59.074 --> 00:04:01.516
"But also like a painting!"

63
00:04:02.677 --> 00:04:06.220
Suddenly she felt bad for picking more flowers than she needed.

64
00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.442
"Mr. Dunn?"

65
00:04:08.883 --> 00:04:09.403
she said.

66
00:04:09.423 --> 00:04:12.406
"I'm sorry I didn't listen to you.

67
00:04:13.847 --> 00:04:17.310
Can I put my extra flowers in water so they don't die right away?"

68
00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:19.812
Mr. Dunn nodded.

69
00:04:19.832 --> 00:04:24.416
"I'm sure you'll be a better listener next time," he said.

70
00:04:25.608 --> 00:04:27.049
"I'll put the flowers in water.

71
00:04:29.211 --> 00:04:31.493
You can keep working on your hammered artwork.

72
00:04:32.594 --> 00:04:33.494
It looks great."

73
00:04:33.514 --> 00:04:35.976
"Thanks," said Izzie.

74
00:04:37.717 --> 00:04:41.180
Izzie carefully picked off a piece of petal that was stuck to the paper.

75
00:04:42.261 --> 00:04:43.722
Mr. Dunn was so nice.

76
00:04:44.883 --> 00:04:48.246
Izzie knew just what to do with her hammered artwork when it was ready.

77
00:04:49.286 --> 00:04:50.687
She was going to give it to Mr.

78
00:04:50.728 --> 00:04:51.068
Dunn!
